      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/19/5161",
      "text": [
        " \"قَالَ رَسُولُ اَللَّهِ صَلَّى اَللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَ آلِهِ : \"مَنْ قُتِلَ دُونَ مَالِهِ فَهُوَ شَهِيدٌ\" \" قَالَ \"وَ قَالَ \"لَوْ كُنْتُ أَنَا لَتَرَكْتُ اَلْمَالَ وَ لَمْ أُقَاتِلْ \" \"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5161 - Al-Alaa narrated from Muhammad ibn Muslim from one of the two Imams (peace be upon them), who said:\n\"The Messenger of Allah (swt) (peace be upon him and his family) said:\n'Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr.'\"\nImam (as) also said: \"If it were me, I would have abandoned the wealth and not fought.\""
        ]
      }
    },
